From 3a32b74add1f4a859cf17eabf7be6f029ebcf3d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:40:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(repair): park identical implementation failures for the
 owner

ai.ubq.fi 300 recorded 53 identical "model run failed (unavailable)"
outcomes over 23 bases, each after a charged reservation. Every recent
cell diagnostic reads model_candidate_unchanged_base: the issue was fixed
upstream (ai.ubq.fi 0c120c11f6) before the first charge, the model
completed without changing its checkout, the trusted committer refused
unchanged_base and the port reported that as unavailable, so the cell
exported a transient provider outage.

Runtime: a completed run that left its checkout unchanged now settles as
"model run completed without any change to its checkout" (stage model,
class semantic_no_progress), still charged ambiguous; every other port
error keeps "model run failed (<kind>)".

Launcher: attempt memory is keyed by base, so it never refused a task
whose base keeps moving. The retry pass now reads it base- and
runtime-independently: three identical outcomes (blocker kind plus a
digest of the normalized message), a transient-class streak only once it
spans the six-hour decay window, park the record in one CAS write as an
explicit owner-gated blocker that no retry rule matches; every later pass
names it. An edited source issue or a changed model route (the
maintenance step now receives the non-secret route selector variables)
re-arms it once; a different signature resets the streak. Charges, intent,
counters and memory are untouched. The 200-reservation cap is now named
instead of skipped silently. Every new shape parses under R80's parsers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01H8mMNvEXtHRiTVR1wJeFLQ
